    lines += ['Captured weapon leech now uses saved fractional fields through shared health/mana consumers; see [source](../tools/reference/weapon-leech-engine-evidence.json) and [native evidence](../tools/reference/weapon-leech-native-evidence.json). Literal older victim-mana behavior and current executable/global-difficulty/event parity remain explicit limits. Shared Crushing Blow preserves fractional victim life and separate resistance truncation, with eligible central missile callbacks before captured-leech life clipping; see [source preparation](../tools/reference/weapon-crushing-engine-evidence.json) and [native evidence](../tools/reference/weapon-crushing-native-evidence.json). The published-guide/older-code Champion/Unique conflict remains explicit; the existing native grouping is retained. Life Tap now uses a distinct fractional defender event before ordinary leech clipping, including outer missiles, native weapon hits, prepared melee and Smite; see [source](../tools/reference/life-tap-engine-evidence.json) and [native evidence](../tools/reference/life-tap-native-evidence.json). Full launch collection, remaining central callbacks, captured defense loss and live prevent-heal still need integration.','']
